    "task": "Record each finished review beside the glosses, with what it saw and its verdict",
    "summary": "Before the agents start, git-gud stamps what they will see (git gloss reviews --stamp); after each successful run it records the report with that stamp (--record), unless --no-record. The bugs and improve prompts now end with a VERDICT line, as git-gloss's honesty prompt does. Depends on git-gloss 0.2.0, which has the reviews command.",
    "groups": [
      {
        "id": "record",
        "intent": "Stamp before the runs, record each successful review after; --no-record",
        "necessity": "required",
        "serves": "task",
        "removal_impact": "reviews would be printed and lost, so a later reader of the branch couldn't see that its glosses were checked",
        "evidence": "Live: a real honesty review of a fixture commit was recorded; git gloss show then marked it reviewed and the branch header counted it",
        "hunks": [
          "h5",
          "h6",
          "h7",
          "h8"
        ],
        "notes": "The stamp names the exact commits the clones are built from (base..sha for a range, the sha otherwise), taken once before any agent runs. Any failure taking it (including non-JSON output) prints a note and costs only the record. Records from one git-gud run are written one at a time (Node runs the synchronous calls in turn); separate processes recording at once are handled by git-gloss's compare-and-swap. Dry runs record nothing."
      },
      {
